--!nonstrict
--[[
	PusherClient v3 — LocalScript for StarterPlayer.StarterPlayerScripts.

	Owns everything the player sees that isn't physics:
	- Locked "through the glass" camera with intro sweep, parallax, idle bob.
	- The game UI, styled after chunky mobile luck-game HUDs: right menu rail
	  (Collection / Upgrades / Galaxy / Shop), tickets chip, Gold Rush event
	  timer, the chip column (quests / warnings / boost timers), the fused
	  DROP PLANET + meteor rush cluster, the near-fullscreen pannable upgrade
	  tree, offer surfaces, and the gacha roller rail.
	- Input: click / tap / Space / gamepad A drops, aimed by cursor or stick.
	- All cosmetic animation: LED chases, marquee wave, bulbs, win line,
	  jackpot odometer, dropper carriage tracking, twin-press mirror + stamp,
	  lane header flashes, the fever tube painter.
	- All shared data/formulas come from ReplicatedStorage.GameConfig — the
	  client keeps ZERO mirrored gameplay tables.

	The machine can be torn down and rebuilt by the server (zone switching),
	so every machine reference lives in `bound`, refilled by bindMachine().
]]

